        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. Trump threatens 100% tariff on French wines unless digital tax dropped Issued on: 16/06/2026 - 12:49 US President Donald Trump has threatened to set a 100 percent tariff on French wine and champagne unless Paris removes a digital services tax on technology firms. France imposed in 2019 a three percent levy on the revenues earned by technology firms - including US giants like Facebook, Amazon, Apple and Google's parent Alphabet - within the country's borders. Eldest son of Norway’s crown princess sentenced to 4 years in prison for rape 16/06/2026 ‘We won’t leave children in the cold’: Lebanese monastery opens doors to displaced 16/06/2026 Trump says Iran deal signed but details remain unclear 16/06/2026 G7 summit: A case of Zelenksy and Europe 'versus Trump'? 16/06/2026 France shuts down twelve Israeli stands at defence trade show 15/06/2026 Middle East Iran war 'has been a strategic disaster for the State of Israel', analyst says 15/06/2026 Middle East US-Iran deal leaves major Lebanon questions unresolved 15/06/2026 Middle East Interim US-Iran peace deal sparks anger among Israelis, who lash out at Netanyahu 15/06/2026 Middle East Iran deal allows Tehran to charge maritime service fees on Hormuz Strait transit, ministry days 15/06/2026 Middle East"
